    "created_at": "2026-03-17T07:08:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-17T07:10:47Z",
    "body": "Hi everyone, I just wanted to share an update regarding this proposal. \n\nI have implemented a demonstration of how the <type-writer> element would function on a live project: https://lumina-port1.netlify.app/about\n\nKey strengths of this implementation:\n1. Performance: The animation is smooth and doesn't cause layout shifts.\n2. Progressive Enhancement: If JavaScript is disabled, the text remains fully visible. Only the animation is skipped, ensuring the content is always available.\n3. Reading Mode Friendly: Since the content is native text, it works perfectly in \"Reading Mode\" or \"Reader View\" across browsers. The animation doesn't interfere with the ability to strip away styles and read the plain text.\n\nI believe a native <type-writer> element would provide a standardized way to handle these animations while maintaining high standards for accessibility and user experience.\n\nLooking forward to your thoughts!",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
