    "created_at": "2026-06-23T12:07:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-23T12:07:48Z",
    "body": "Hey @anafibnshahibul thanks for the proposal. This is an interesting element, I've definitely seen a few of these around before, there's even prior art from GitHub with the [typing-effect-element](https://github.com/github/typing-effect-element).\n\nIn terms of getting this into the standard, I think this is probably something we'd want to add as pure css. It's purely visual and offers no semantic improvement to HTML. Therefore I'd recommend [raising an issue with the css working group](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/new) and exploring it there. The design would likely take the shape of additional properties, and would not impact the DOM tree, therefore the a11y tree.\n\nOn this grounds, I'll close this as not planned here, and perhaps if you do raise an issue with the csswg, you could reference this issue?",
